{
  "sn55.1:0.1": "Linked Discourses 55.1 ",
  "sn55.1:0.2": "1. At Bamboo Gate ",
  "sn55.1:0.3": "A Wheel-Turning Monarch ",
  "sn55.1:1.1": "At Sāvatthī. ",
  "sn55.1:1.2": "There the Buddha … said: ",
  "sn55.1:1.3": "“Mendicants, suppose a wheel-turning monarch were to rule as sovereign lord over these four continents. And when his body breaks up, after death, he’s reborn in a good place, a heavenly realm, in the company of the gods of the thirty-three. There he amuses himself in the Garden of Delight, escorted by a band of nymphs, and supplied and provided with the five kinds of heavenly sensual stimulation. Still, as he’s lacking four things, he’s not exempt from hell, the animal realm, or the ghost realm. He’s not exempt from places of loss, bad places, the underworld. ",
  "sn55.1:1.4": "Now suppose a noble disciple wears rags and feeds on scraps of almsfood. Still, as they have four things, they’re exempt from hell, the animal realm, or the ghost realm. They’re exempt from places of loss, bad places, the underworld. ",
  "sn55.1:2.1": "What four? ",
  "sn55.1:2.2": "It’s when a noble disciple has experiential confidence in the Buddha: ",
  "sn55.1:2.3": "‘That Blessed One is perfected, a fully awakened Buddha, accomplished in knowledge and conduct, holy, knower of the world, supreme guide for those fit for training, teacher of gods and humans, awakened, blessed.’ ",
  "sn55.1:2.4": "They have experiential confidence in the teaching: ",
